# The companion asserts two brand colours in PHP, because a module may not read
# a file and a provider may not read one at boot. Its own suite checks those two
# against this copy of the brand's token file; this row is what keeps the copy
# equal to the brand's own, so the two checks in series mean the application
# paints what the brand says and not what somebody typed.

32548c774fa39f2614094826cc6c77bc35a2cce244df6b817ead2e200518ca5c  app-modules/design/resources/tokens.json  brand:tokens/tokens.json

# The accessibility page measures the palette rather than quoting it, so the
# spec needs the palette in its own tree: a generator cannot reach another
# repository, and the three ratios that went wrong here went wrong precisely
# because nothing local could be checked against.

32548c774fa39f2614094826cc6c77bc35a2cce244df6b817ead2e200518ca5c  60-brand/tokens.json  brand:tokens/tokens.json

# Home Assistant shows an integration's icon and logo from the PNG files in its own
# `brand/` directory, so the integration carries the brand's exports for it.

